{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for reporting this. Your account and mailbox are healthy, so this is most likely a shared mailbox connection issue in Outlook. Please try these steps: 1) Fully close and reopen Outlook on your computer (BL-DT-0108). Shared mailboxes are added automatically once access applies. 2) If orders@ still does not appear, open Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com) and check whether orders@ is listed there, using Add shared folder or mailbox if needed. Then reply and let us know: whether orders@ shows up in Outlook on the web, and whether your manager or the orders@ mailbox owner has recently given you access to it. If it still will not show after restarting, we will add it manually or check the access request. Note that your computer currently shows as offline, so please make sure it is on and connected when you try the restart.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user for james.oconnor@brightline.example (user_id 8): account active, not blocked, no failed logins, mailbox 29.7% used (15.2 GB of 50 GB), so mailbox-full is ruled out. Device BL-DT-0108 (Windows 11) is listed as offline, last check-in 2026-10-11 00:58 UTC, no disk or other warnings. Per KB-011, the next steps are to confirm the user was granted access and to have them restart Outlook or check Outlook on the web. I have no tool to view mailbox delegation, so I could not verify whether orders@ access was granted. If the user confirms they were never granted access, this needs mailbox owner approval, then Tier 2 makes the change (KB-006). Also note that orders@ needs a separate Send As permission for sending. No actions were queued. Awaiting user reply on OWA visibility and access grant status.",
